Subject: [PATCH] player: use pure black background instead of theme surface color

The player root container painted the Material3 ColorScheme `background`
(#141218 in the dark scheme) behind the video surface. The video is a
proportionally centered SurfaceView, so on displays wider than 16:9
(3:2, 16:10, ...) the uncovered area showed this dark gray-blue band
instead of pure black, which reads as a glowing gray letterbox bar.

The sampled pixels of the official build confirm it:
  letterbox bar : rgb(20, 17, 24)
  real video black : rgb(0, 0, 0)

So this is not a limited/full range mismatch - the app simply drew a
non-black background.

Compose Color is an inline value class storing 0xAARRGGBB in the upper
32 bits of a long, so opaque black is 0xff00000000000000L.

--- a/smali/e47.smali
+++ b/smali/e47.smali
@@ -14142,7 +14142,7 @@
     move/from16 p6, v2
 
     .line 86
-    iget-wide v1, v4, Lty0;->E:J
+    const-wide v1, 0xff00000000000000L
 
     .line 87
     sget-object v4, Lgn3;->J0:Lt83;
